prompt:
Design an internal workbench where authorized users can create versioned prompt templates, choose an approved model configuration, run a small test set, compare two immutable experiment runs, and share a read-only result link with their team. Prompts and test data may contain sensitive text.

State the API and durable entities, then cover:

- immutable prompt and model-parameter versions, versus editable drafts;
- asynchronous execution, streaming progress, cancellation, retries, and cost/concurrency limits;
- reproducible comparisons when models, templates, and test sets change;
- redaction, tenant access control, auditability, and retention; and
- evaluation metrics and failure signals that distinguish model quality from platform health.

Do not design model training or a public end-user chat product.
